# Siren Guard — AI Rules

## Project Context

- **Type**: macOS desktop utility (menu bar + floating overlay)
- **Stack**: Electron · plain HTML/CSS/JS renderer · electron-store · Bun
- **Repo layout**:
  ```
  main.js           # Electron main: tray, window, lock IPC
  preload.js        # contextBridge IPC bridge
  store.js          # electron-store wrapper
  renderer/         # floating button UI
  assets/           # tray icon, button glyph
  ```

---

## Workflow

- Always follow: **Research → Plan → Execute**
- Do not write code until the plan is confirmed if the change touches 2+ files
- For ambiguous tasks: ask, do not guess
- Commit style: Conventional Commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, `refactor:`, `test:`)
- Package manager: **Bun** (`bun install`, `bun start`, `bun add`) — do not use npm
- Use `/specsmd-fire-planner` before multi-file feature work; implement via `/specsmd-fire-builder`

---

## Code Rules

- Plain JavaScript in main/preload/renderer — no TypeScript unless explicitly approved
- Never rewrite an entire file to change one function — surgical edits only
- Match existing naming conventions and indentation exactly
- Remove all AI-style comments before finishing
- Remove unused imports and variables before finalizing

---

## Constraints

- No new external dependencies without explicit approval
- macOS-only lock logic for v1 (`CGSession -suspend` via `child_process.exec`)
- Terminal commands: check mentally before suggesting — no destructive defaults
- Never expose secrets, tokens, or credentials in output

---

## Project-Specific Notes

- Floating window uses `-webkit-app-region: drag` on the wrapper and `no-drag` on the click target to support drag + click
- Use a short mouse-down/mouse-up threshold to distinguish drag from click
- Lock screen via `CGSession -suspend` — does not require accessibility permissions
- Button position and launch-at-login settings persist via `electron-store`
- Idle button: translucent/low-opacity; armed state: pulse/countdown during 2s cancel window

---

## Out of Scope

- Authentication / multi-user support
- Cloud sync
- Mobile version
- Cross-platform lock (Windows/Linux) in v1
- Multiple trigger types, settings screen, stats — post-v1 roadmap only
- Analytics/tracking beyond optional local trigger count
